## 5. RNN vs Transformer: Direct Comparison

| Dimension | RNN | Transformer |
|-----------|-----|-------------|
| **Weight matrices** | One matrix (W_h) does everything | Three specialised matrices (W_Q, W_K, W_V) |
| **Processing order** | Sequential — one token at a time, each waits for previous | Parallel — all tokens processed simultaneously |
| **Memory format** | Single fixed-size hidden state vector, overwritten at each step | Every token retains its own separate Q, K, V vectors throughout |
| **Access to "How" when processing "live?"** | ~8% of original signal, buried in compressed h₅ | 100% of original signal, directly accessible via attention |
| **Speed (100 tokens)** | ~1 second (sequential, 10ms per step) | One parallel pass on GPU (milliseconds) |
| **Context length** | Struggles beyond 20–30 words | Handles 100,000+ tokens |
| **Likely output for our example** | *"Cats live a wonderful life"* (lost duration instruction) | *"Cats typically live 12 to 18 years"* (full context preserved) |

